# /wall is now the site's canonical home (pages/index.tsx renders the same
# component as pages/wall.tsx). This is a permanent redirect so the old URL
# doesn't compete with / as duplicate content and old links/bookmarks land
# on the real canonical address.
/wall  /  301

# PLAN-PRODUCTION-ROUTE-ALLOWLIST.md: the production export (next.config.js
# exportPathMap) ships only /, /about, /contact, /journal, and /journal/*
# (one entry per posts/*.md slug). Netlify serves a real file for those
# (and this rule is only consulted when no matching file exists), so this
# single catch-all sends every other route — /abstract, /thoughts/*,
# /black-hole, /synth-archive, the *-lab sandboxes, /admin, and any future
# page added to pages/ without also being added to PRODUCTION_ROUTES — to
# the canonical home instead of a hard 404. Covers new excluded pages
# automatically; nothing to maintain here when a page is added to or
# removed from source.
/*  /  301
